1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,726
Government services can be difficult to navigate.

2
00:00:02,726 --> 00:00:07,400
JANSAHAY makes the journey simpler, starting with what the citizen actually needs.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:17,400
Instead of searching through departments, the citizen simply describes their goal.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:29,400
JANSAHAY asks a few simple questions and shows exactly what documents are needed.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,643
The citizen uploads the required documents and submits the application.

6
00:00:37,643 --> 00:00:42,229
A Case Passport is created immediately.

7
00:00:42,229 --> 00:00:51,400
The citizen can see where the case is and what happens next.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,400
Behind the scenes, the case moves through the right officers.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,200
Technically, JANSAHAY uses one case engine and one workflow engine.

10
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:14,400
The same system can support certificates, EPFO claims, and grievances.

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,306
Security is enforced on the server.

12
00:01:19,306 --> 00:01:28,635
Officers only see cases and actions allowed for their role, department, and jurisdiction.

13
00:01:28,635 --> 00:01:31,506
Invalid actions are rejected.

14
00:01:31,506 --> 00:01:39,400
Every important workflow action is recorded in a tamper-evident audit history.

15
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,608
AI helps with service discovery and simple explanations.

16
00:01:44,608 --> 00:01:49,216
It cannot approve, reject, or change a case.

17
00:01:49,216 --> 00:01:54,400
This prototype uses synthetic data and mocked government integrations.

18
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,680
JANSAHAY puts the citizen's journey first.

